      "text": "The holiday season now surrounds us at every turn. Christmas trees glow in offices and homes, carols echo in malls and building lobbies, and parties fill calendars well into late evenings. Traffic slows to a crawl as shoppers crowd commercial centers and families travel to reunite. In the rush to celebrate, days grow longer, nights shorter, and rest becomes a luxury many willingly sacrifice.\n#MBOpinions\n\nREAD: https://t.co/wHw7zkISzk",
